    {
      "segment_id": "S00001",
      "start_char": 0,
      "end_char": 213,
      "text": "MEXICO\nSTATISTICAL ISSUES\nI. Assessment of Data Adequacy for Surveillance\nGeneral: Data provision is adequate for surveillance.\nNational accounts: The national accounts follow the recommendations of the System of\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00002",
      "start_char": 213,
      "end_char": 381,
      "text": "National Accounts, 2008 (2008 SNA). Economic activities, products, household final\nconsumption expenditure, and government final consumption expenditure are classified\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00003",
      "start_char": 381,
      "end_char": 571,
      "text": "according to updated international classifications. Data sources and statistical techniques are\nrobust. A wide range of source data is available, including economic censuses conducted every\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00004",
      "start_char": 571,
      "end_char": 761,
      "text": "five years and a vast program of monthly and annual surveys, administrative data, as well as a\nbusiness register of economic units that is regularly updated. INEGI (the National Statistical\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00005",
      "start_char": 761,
      "end_char": 952,
      "text": "Office) disseminates annual and quarterly GDP statistics, sectoral accounts, and balance sheets.\nThe 2021 data ROSC update found that the national accounts are of a high quality. Since 2015,\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00006",
      "start_char": 952,
      "end_char": 1132,
      "text": "Mexico has made significant improvements on the methodological and dissemination aspects\nof data quality. There are still some areas for further improvements, such as implementing\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00007",
      "start_char": 1132,
      "end_char": 1311,
      "text": "chained GDP volume indices with previous period annual weights, the treatment of goods for\nprocessing abroad, and the coverage of illegal activities. In addition, some government\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00008",
      "start_char": 1311,
      "end_char": 1498,
      "text": "transactions on a quarterly basis are recorded on a cash basis rather than on an accrual basis.\nThe ROSC mission identified the need for greater consistency in data recording between the\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00009",
      "start_char": 1498,
      "end_char": 1683,
      "text": "Bank of Mexico (Banxico), and the Ministry of Finance (SHCP) and for regular reconciliation\nexercises among compilers to resolve some discrepancies involving data on the public sector.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00010",
      "start_char": 1683,
      "end_char": 1864,
      "text": "Three technical assistance missions took place over the past fiscal year; two on developing a\npreliminary work plan to implement the use of chain-linked volume measures in economic\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00011",
      "start_char": 1864,
      "end_char": 2098,
      "text": "surveys and national accounts; and one with Banxico, SHCP, and INEGI on harmonization of\nnational accounts and government finance statistics.\nPrices: The concepts and definitions for both the CPI and PPI meet international standards.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00012",
      "start_char": 2098,
      "end_char": 2269,
      "text": "The CPI reference period is the second half of July 2018, and the basket is based on\ninformation from the National Survey of Household Expenditure 2012 and 2013, the 2014\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00013",
      "start_char": 2269,
      "end_char": 2449,
      "text": "Household Income and Expenditure Survey, and the 1999 COICOP classification. The PPI\nreference period is July 2019, and the basket of goods and weighting structure is based on the\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00014",
      "start_char": 2449,
      "end_char": 2675,
      "text": "Economic Censuses and the System of National Accounts. The PPI covers agricultural,\nmanufacturing, construction, and services sectors, which account for 79.2 percent of Mexican\nproduction. It excludes trade and some services.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00015",
      "start_char": 2675,
      "end_char": 2860,
      "text": "Government finance statistics: Fiscal statistics are comprehensive and timely, except for the\nsubnational sector. The authorities compile fiscal statistics following national concepts,\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00016",
      "start_char": 2860,
      "end_char": 3049,
      "text": "definitions, and classifications to support domestic policy needs. The authorities also compile\nfiscal statistics in alignment with the Government Finance Statistics Manual (GFSM2014). The\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00017",
      "start_char": 3049,
      "end_char": 3224,
      "text": "2021 Data ROSC mission pointed out that, while source data used for the national and\ninternational (GFSM2014) presentations are the same, differences in the classification of\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00018",
      "start_char": 3224,
      "end_char": 3347,
      "text": "transactions and coverage of institutional units make it difficult for users to reconcile the\nINTERNATIONAL MONETARY FUND 5"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "schema_version": "locator_index_v1",
  "source_id": "MAC-010",
  "source_sha256": "8fac4146590dbe2ed458f7356748f5880d021e03cc4982b1e7efe083d33f622a",
  "locator": "page 101",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "S00001",
      "start_char": 0,
      "end_char": 195,
      "text": "MEXICO\ndifferent presentations. It recommended publishing a table of all institutional units in the\npublic sector and its subsectors, clearly grouping them according to: 1) the coverage of units\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00002",
      "start_char": 195,
      "end_char": 386,
      "text": "used in the national presentation; 2) the coverage used in the international presentation; and\n3) the subsectors of the public sector as described in the GFSM2014. A full adoption of uniform\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00003",
      "start_char": 386,
      "end_char": 624,
      "text": "accounting standards at the sub-national level would help obtain an improved measure of\npublic fixed investment in the national accounts.\nPension liabilities are partially reported, while government securities are reported at face value.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00004",
      "start_char": 624,
      "end_char": 846,
      "text": "The official debt statistics do not include the stock of T-bonds issued to the Bank of Mexico\n(Banxico) for liquidity management purposes, and the accounting practices adopted by the\nfederal government and Banxico differ.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00005",
      "start_char": 846,
      "end_char": 1029,
      "text": "Monetary and financial statistics: The methodological foundations of monetary statistics are\ngenerally sound. Availability of data on other financial intermediaries such as insurance\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00006",
      "start_char": 1029,
      "end_char": 1214,
      "text": "companies and pension funds allow for the construction of a financial corporation’s survey\nwith full coverage of the Mexican financial system. Mexico reports data on some indicators of\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00007",
      "start_char": 1214,
      "end_char": 1396,
      "text": "the Financial Access Survey (FAS), including gender disaggregated data on the use of basic\nfinancial services and the two indicators (commercial bank branches per 100,000 adults and\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00008",
      "start_char": 1396,
      "end_char": 1584,
      "text": "ATMs per 100,000 adults) adopted by the UN to monitor Target 8.10 of the Sustainable\nDevelopment Goals.\nFinancial sector surveillance: Mexico regularly reports monthly Financial Soundness\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00009",
      "start_char": 1584,
      "end_char": 1759,
      "text": "Indicators (FSIs) to the IMF for publication. Currently, Mexico reports 14 core and 9\nencouraged indicators for deposit takers, 2 additional FSI for OFCs,1 additional FSI for\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00010",
      "start_char": 1759,
      "end_char": 1946,
      "text": "households and 1 additional FSI for real estate markets. FSIs on the non-financial corporate\nsector are not reported. Reporting has been temporarily interrupted following the publication\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00011",
      "start_char": 1946,
      "end_char": 2132,
      "text": "of May 2021 data in order to revise historical and current data according to IFRS9 standards\nand is expected to resume by the end of the year. The authorities have periodically produced\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00012",
      "start_char": 2132,
      "end_char": 2291,
      "text": "updated FSIs in the interim according to the old standard on request.\nExternal sector statistics (ESS): The 2021 data ROSC update found that ESS are of a high\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00013",
      "start_char": 2291,
      "end_char": 2472,
      "text": "quality. In 2017, Banxico migrated the BOP and IIP statistics to the Balance of Payments and\nInternational Investment Position Manual (BPM6), sixth edition, with the publication of\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00014",
      "start_char": 2472,
      "end_char": 2659,
      "text": "quarterly BPM6-based BOP data and IIP data . The External Debt Statistics, Guide for Compilers\nand Users, 2013 (EDS Guide) is yet to be fully implemented. Remaining issues relate to: (i)\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00015",
      "start_char": 2659,
      "end_char": 2841,
      "text": "including the intercompany external debt and SDR allocations in external debt statistics\ndisseminated by Banxico; (ii) extending the market valuation of liabilities to all financial\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00016",
      "start_char": 2841,
      "end_char": 2993,
      "text": "institutions (some external debt are presented at face value); and (iii) recording the interest of\nthe public sector external debt on an accrual basis.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00017",
      "start_char": 2993,
      "end_char": 3173,
      "text": "Consistency could be improved between the IIP and external debt. There are also differences\nbetween the balance of payments and national accounts, notably in the financial account\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00018",
      "start_char": 3173,
      "end_char": 3354,
      "text": "transactions and positions. The authorities participate in the coordinated direct investment\nsurvey and coordinated portfolio investment survey and disseminate the data template on\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00019",
      "start_char": 3354,
      "end_char": 3496,
      "text": "international reserves and foreign currency liquidity (reserve template) and quarterly external\ndebt statistics.\n6 INTERNATIONAL MONETARY FUND"
    }
  ]
}
